1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,709
One thousand rupees at ten percent per annum. Compounded

2
00:00:03,709 --> 00:00:06,318
every year, that money becomes one thousand one hundred

3
00:00:06,318 --> 00:00:09,043
rupees after one year. But the same ten percent

4
00:00:09,043 --> 00:00:12,680
compounded half-yearly gives one thousand fifty rupees after six

5
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,780
months, and one thousand one hundred two rupees and

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:19,420
fifty paise after a year. Same money, same rate,

7
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:23,571
more interest. Why does the timing change the answer?

8
00:00:24,337 --> 00:00:27,442
First, the conversion period. The conversion period is the

9
00:00:27,442 --> 00:00:32,317
time interval after which the interest is added to

10
00:00:32,317 --> 00:00:34,627
the principal. If interest is added once a year,

11
00:00:34,627 --> 00:00:37,337
the period is one full year: one turn of

12
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:41,097
the clock. If it is added every six months,

13
00:00:41,097 --> 00:00:44,071
that same year is cut into two equal periods.

14
00:00:44,071 --> 00:00:46,458
And if it is added every three months, the

15
00:00:46,458 --> 00:00:48,666
year becomes four quarter periods. So the conversion period

16
00:00:48,666 --> 00:00:51,497
fixes two things together, the rate for each period

17
00:00:51,497 --> 00:00:52,768
and how many periods there are.

18
00:00:53,393 --> 00:00:57,029
Now the half-yearly rule. When the conversion period halves,

19
00:00:57,029 --> 00:00:59,017
two things change at the same time. The rate

20
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:03,433
for each period halves as well: R becomes R

21
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:08,413
divided by two. And the number of periods doubles:

22
00:01:08,413 --> 00:01:11,235
n becomes two n. So the amount is P

23
00:01:11,235 --> 00:01:13,867
times one plus R over two hundred, all raised

24
00:01:13,867 --> 00:01:18,648
to two n. Ten percent per annum compounded half-yearly

25
00:01:18,648 --> 00:01:22,313
means five percent for each half-year, never ten percent

26
00:01:22,313 --> 00:01:26,544
every six months, and never change the exponent alone.

27
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:30,320
Let us work it out. Principal one thousand rupees,

28
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:34,800
rate ten percent per annum, time one year, compounded

29
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:38,243
half-yearly. The rate for each half-year is ten divided

30
00:01:38,243 --> 00:01:41,100
by two, that is five percent. And one year

31
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:44,339
holds two half-yearly periods. So the amount is one

32
00:01:44,339 --> 00:01:46,802
thousand times one point zero five squared, which is

33
00:01:46,802 --> 00:01:51,760
one thousand one hundred two rupees and fifty paise.

34
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,280
The compound interest is one thousand one hundred two

35
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:56,820
point five minus one thousand, that is one hundred

36
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,031
two rupees and fifty paise.

37
00:01:59,683 --> 00:02:02,026
A year has four quarters. So when interest is

38
00:02:02,026 --> 00:02:06,003
compounded quarterly, the rate for one period becomes R

39
00:02:06,003 --> 00:02:10,643
divided by four, and the number of periods becomes

40
00:02:10,643 --> 00:02:12,274
four n. The amount is P times one plus

41
00:02:12,274 --> 00:02:14,803
R over four hundred, all raised to four n.

42
00:02:14,803 --> 00:02:19,583
This is the same conversion-period rule, extended from two

43
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:22,243
periods to four. The rate and the number of

44
00:02:22,243 --> 00:02:24,274
periods always change together.

45
00:02:24,877 --> 00:02:28,660
The same structure answers questions about population. A village

46
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,677
has six thousand two hundred and fifty people, and

47
00:02:31,677 --> 00:02:36,537
the population grows by eight percent every year. After

48
00:02:36,537 --> 00:02:39,557
one year the population is six thousand two hundred

49
00:02:39,557 --> 00:02:41,960
and fifty times one point zero eight, and that

50
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,877
new total becomes the base for the next year.

51
00:02:44,877 --> 00:02:47,505
So after two years the population is six thousand

52
00:02:47,505 --> 00:02:49,931
two hundred and fifty times one point zero eight

53
00:02:49,931 --> 00:02:53,577
squared, which is seven thousand two hundred and ninety.

54
00:02:53,577 --> 00:02:57,047
A repeated percentage increase is exactly the same structure

55
00:02:57,047 --> 00:02:58,388
as compound interest.

56
00:02:59,030 --> 00:03:04,054
Now depreciation, the mirror image. Depreciation is a reduction

57
00:03:04,054 --> 00:03:05,835
in the value of an article due to use

58
00:03:05,835 --> 00:03:09,208
and age. A quantity that loses R percent in

59
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:13,041
each period keeps one hundred minus R percent. Ten

60
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:16,830
percent off leaves ninety percent, and the next reduction

61
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:20,102
is taken from the new value. So after two

62
00:03:20,102 --> 00:03:22,236
periods the value is P times zero point nine

63
00:03:22,236 --> 00:03:25,175
squared, and in general V is P times one

64
00:03:25,175 --> 00:03:27,986
minus R over one hundred, all raised to n.

65
00:03:27,986 --> 00:03:31,226
A ball dropped from twenty five metres loses ten

66
00:03:31,226 --> 00:03:35,290
percent of its height at each bounce, so after

67
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:38,097
two bounces it rises to twenty five times zero

68
00:03:38,097 --> 00:03:41,601
point nine squared, that is twenty point two five metres.

69
00:03:42,170 --> 00:03:45,439
One structure, three uses. Money at compound interest and

70
00:03:45,439 --> 00:03:48,202
population growth both use P times one plus r,

71
00:03:48,202 --> 00:03:51,578
all raised to n. Depreciation uses P times one

72
00:03:51,578 --> 00:03:55,010
minus r, raised to n. A growth multiplier is

73
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:58,275
greater than one, and a depreciation multiplier is less

74
00:03:58,275 --> 00:04:02,250
than one. So keep two decisions separate: how often

75
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:06,161
the update happens, and whether the quantity rises or falls.

76
00:04:06,773 --> 00:04:10,373
Here is the decision map. Step one: identify the

77
00:04:10,373 --> 00:04:13,853
conversion period. Step two: find the rate for one

78
00:04:13,853 --> 00:04:18,893
period. Step three: count the number of periods. Step

79
00:04:18,893 --> 00:04:22,793
four: choose plus for growth, or minus for decrease.

80
00:04:22,793 --> 00:04:26,547
Step five: apply that factor again and again. Period,

81
00:04:26,547 --> 00:04:30,784
rate, factor, repeat: that is the whole method.

82
00:04:31,427 --> 00:04:35,106
Your turn. Three questions. First: twelve thousand rupees at

83
00:04:35,106 --> 00:04:36,936
ten percent per annum for one and a half

84
00:04:36,936 --> 00:04:40,853
years, compounded half-yearly. Find the amount. Second: twelve percent

85
00:04:40,853 --> 00:04:44,947
per annum for two years, compounded quarterly. What is

86
00:04:44,947 --> 00:04:47,764
the rate for each period, and how many periods

87
00:04:47,764 --> 00:04:52,076
are there? Third: a television costing twenty one thousand

88
00:04:52,076 --> 00:04:55,235
rupees depreciates by five percent in one year. What

89
00:04:55,235 --> 00:04:59,307
is it worth now? And a quick check: for

90
00:04:59,307 --> 00:05:02,189
eight percent growth, which factor do you use, and

91
00:05:02,189 --> 00:05:04,778
for eight percent depreciation, which factor?

92
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:18,071
Let us check. For A, the rate is five

93
00:05:18,071 --> 00:05:20,322
percent per half-year and one and a half years

94
00:05:20,322 --> 00:05:22,900
is three periods, so the amount is twelve thousand

95
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,240
times one point zero five cubed, that is thirteen

96
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:29,140
thousand eight hundred ninety one rupees and fifty paise.

97
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,475
For B, twelve divided by four is three percent

98
00:05:32,475 --> 00:05:35,660
per quarter, and two years is eight quarters, so

99
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:37,700
the amount is P times one point zero three

100
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:41,170
raised to eight. For C, five percent depreciation leaves

101
00:05:41,170 --> 00:05:44,325
ninety five percent, so twenty one thousand times zero

102
00:05:44,325 --> 00:05:46,674
point nine five is nineteen thousand nine hundred and

103
00:05:46,674 --> 00:05:50,347
fifty rupees. And the quick check: for eight percent

104
00:05:50,347 --> 00:05:52,470
growth use one point zero eight, and for eight

105
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:55,878
percent depreciation use zero point nine two, because one

106
00:05:55,878 --> 00:05:58,571
minus zero point zero eight is zero point nine two.

107
00:05:59,092 --> 00:06:01,016
Let us gather the whole lesson in one place.

108
00:06:01,016 --> 00:06:04,672
The conversion period has three cases: annually, the rate

109
00:06:04,672 --> 00:06:07,022
is R and there are n periods; half-yearly, the

110
00:06:07,022 --> 00:06:09,432
rate is R over two and the periods double

111
00:06:09,432 --> 00:06:14,112
to two n; quarterly, the rate is R over

112
00:06:14,112 --> 00:06:17,592
four and the periods become four n. Growth uses

113
00:06:17,592 --> 00:06:19,748
A equals P times one plus R over one

114
00:06:19,748 --> 00:06:23,134
hundred, all raised to n: that is compound interest

115
00:06:23,134 --> 00:06:27,282
and population. Depreciation uses V equals P times one

116
00:06:27,282 --> 00:06:30,048
minus R over one hundred, all raised to n:

117
00:06:30,048 --> 00:06:33,252
the value keeps what is left. And the five

118
00:06:33,252 --> 00:06:37,032
steps: identify the conversion period, find the rate for

119
00:06:37,032 --> 00:06:40,058
one period, count the number of periods, choose plus

120
00:06:40,058 --> 00:06:43,572
for growth or minus for decrease, and apply that

121
00:06:43,572 --> 00:06:44,963
factor again and again.

122
00:06:45,598 --> 00:06:49,778
One last look. The compounding clock: annually, half-yearly, quarterly,

123
00:06:49,778 --> 00:06:53,678
with the rate and the number of periods changing

124
00:06:53,678 --> 00:06:57,289
together. Growth uses P times one plus R over

125
00:06:57,289 --> 00:07:00,878
one hundred, all raised to n, and depreciation uses

126
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:03,437
P times one minus R over one hundred, raised

127
00:07:03,437 --> 00:07:08,398
to n. Keep the two decisions separate: how often,

128
00:07:08,398 --> 00:07:14,117
and up or down. Period, rate, factor, repeat. Thank

129
00:07:14,117 --> 00:07:16,489
you for watching, and see you in the next lesson.
